    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "But some people argue that without strong enforcement first, you can't have a stable system at all—that the humanitarian approach actually causes more chaos at the border by encouraging more people to try to cross. Doesn't that concern about national security and the rule of law make the enforcement approach more foundational for long-term stability?",
